## Additional notice: content pulled or promoted via this tool is unvetted

This package (`open-wheel`) is a tool for creating, searching, and exchanging
"wheel" entries (design decisions, failure records, reusable code) between
repositories, including directly between peers via `open-wheel pull <src>`.

**Peer-to-peer and cross-namespace exchange is not moderated by this project.**
Content obtained via `pull` from any source you specify — official, personal,
or third-party — is not scanned, vetted, or endorsed by the maintainers of
this tool. It may be inaccurate, outdated, or (in adversarial cases) crafted
to mislead an AI agent reading it (prompt injection). You are solely
responsible for evaluating the trustworthiness of any source you `pull` from
and for reviewing generated rules/entries before relying on them.

This tool does not execute untrusted code: `pull`/`promote` only read and
write Markdown/JSON text files. It does not run, evaluate, or install
anything from a pulled source. Nonetheless, text surfaced to an AI agent as
"advice" can still influence that agent's behavior — treat pulled sources
with the same caution you would apply to any unreviewed instructions from a
third party.
